# Spec-driven workflow

- Before planning or coding, read `specs/000-product/` and any relevant `specs/NNN-*/` folder.
- Prefer committed specs over chat memory when they conflict.
- New features: copy `.cursor/skills/spec-driven-design/templates/` into `specs/NNN-name/`, fill overview → requirements → architecture → tasks, then implement.
- Behavior or design changes must update the matching spec in the same change set.
- Leave unknowns as `TBD`; do not invent product requirements.
- For the full workflow, use the project skill `spec-driven-design`.
